  "text": "Climate sensitivity is a key measure in climate science and describes how much Earth's surface will warm in response to a doubling of the atmospheric carbon dioxide (CO2) concentration. Its formal definition is: \"The change in the surface temperature in response to a change in the atmospheric carbon dioxide (CO2) concentration or other radiative forcing.\" This concept helps scientists understand the extent and magnitude of the effects of climate change.",
